		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=42288#p42288"><![CDATA[
Then there is corotational FEM which can be done realtime. The algorithm complexity of this solver is dominated by the CG method as in David Baraff's cloth solver.<br><br>You can apply the same constraint satisfaction technique described in Baraff's solver to a corotational FEM solver.<br><br>For cloth it seems that there is a specific FEM solver described in this paper:<br><br><a href="https://animation.rwth-aachen.de/media/papers/2013-CAG-AdaptiveCloth.pdf" class="postlink">https://animation.rwth-aachen.de/media/ ... eCloth.pdf</a><br><br>It's important to remember that corotational FEM is considered by many as state of the art soft body simulation for games.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11211">irlanrobson</a> — Fri Jul 26, 2019 4:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
